{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The 1/4-20 screws could complement my UNC rivet nuts for assemblies needing flush heads, provided the length fits my project.",
    "Gloves and large utility syringes connect naturally to my resin and adhesive work by helping with cleanup and controlled liquid transfer, subject to material compatibility."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The wire connectors, pipe fittings, pneumatic valve and pressure gauge require specific jobs and connection sizes that my recent purchases do not establish.",
    "Another wood screw assortment duplicates supplies I already have, while the mesh needs a definite application before I would buy it. Knife-making steel assumes a specialized project I have not shown interest in."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Owning workshop tools seems to have been treated as a reason to want supplies for wiring, plumbing and pneumatics, even though those tasks need separate evidence.",
    "My purchases of fastener assortments seem to have been read as an ongoing need for more assortments, without considering what I already have."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Useful additions need to fit my existing supplies: thread standard, screw length, head shape and material compatibility matter more than a general workshop connection.",
    "I distinguish between something that could be useful someday and something that supports work I can do now; a plausible use alone does not make mesh or another screw kit an immediate choice."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my fabrication and resin work but stretch that interest into unrelated workshop tasks and duplicate supplies."
}"}
